;;; The twin of `wild-in-match.ein` — M1e2 **W20**, banked by S1e2.2.20
;;; (2026-11-05): the same program with the wildcard `_` written as `?any`, a
;;; variable the rule reads nowhere else. Its answer is the witness's right
;;; one: `w` fires on `(holds a)`, root holds `(hit w)`, and R is
;;; `{(hit w)}` and `{(hit a), (hit w)}` (`ein solve FILE` at `c73a0796`,
;;; release and debug).

(relation holds Node) (relation hit Node)
(holds a)
(rule w () :match (holds ?any) :assert (hit w))
